1
00:00:00,214 --> 00:00:03,888
Meet Gambit: chess you can play
and understand inside Hermes.

2
00:00:04,689 --> 00:00:06,614
Make your move in the terminal.

3
00:00:06,614 --> 00:00:10,339
A live status follows Hermes
as it prepares one reply,

4
00:00:10,339 --> 00:00:11,695
then the board updates.

5
00:00:18,489 --> 00:00:20,799
Need a nudge? Ask for a hint.

6
00:00:20,799 --> 00:00:23,703
Start with a clue that leaves
the move yours to find.

7
00:00:27,493 --> 00:00:29,443
Ask again for more detail.

8
00:00:29,443 --> 00:00:31,541
You choose when to reveal the next hint.

9
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:38,285
In Coach mode, Hermes reviews
the move you just played.

10
00:00:38,285 --> 00:00:42,635
Stockfish analysis explains what changed
and why it matters.

11
00:00:42,635 --> 00:00:46,075
Here, pushing the g-pawn exposed
the king to checkmate.

12
00:00:53,468 --> 00:00:56,996
Choose Normal mode for a quiet game,
with help when you ask.

13
00:00:59,489 --> 00:01:01,064
Bring your own history.

14
00:01:01,064 --> 00:01:04,714
Find the exact Chess.com match
and open it in replay.

15
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:11,885
Follow the original line,
or try another move.

16
00:01:11,885 --> 00:01:15,787
Practice the alternative while
your imported game stays intact.

17
00:01:21,364 --> 00:01:23,714
Play a game. Understand a decision.

18
00:01:23,809 --> 00:01:26,934
Try another line.
Gambit, built for Hermes.
